{
  "slug": "artist:wizkid",
  "name": "Wizkid",
  "editorial_article": "Ayodeji Ibrahim Balogun, known as Wizkid, began his music career at 11 in Lagos, Nigeria, recording early material as Lil Prinz before finding prominence with his 2011 debut album Superstar on Empire Mates Entertainment. His international breakout arrived in 2016 when he featured on Drake’s One Dance, a global number-one hit that established him as a key figure in modern Afrobeats. Subsequent work, including the 2020 album Made in Lagos, saw the artist reach new heights with the single Essence, featuring Tems, which became the first Nigerian song to chart on the Billboard Hot 100. Over his career, Wizkid has bridged global pop with African rhythmic foundations, collaborating with artists ranging from Beyoncé on The Lion King: The Gift to Justin Bieber and Brent Faiyaz, while managing his own imprint, Starboy Entertainment.",
